{"name":"US Field Drab","hex":"#716140","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"},{"term":"drab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fabric, usually of thick cotton or wool, having a dull brownish yellow, dull grey, or dun colour.","The color of this fabric."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the color of some types of drabcloth: dull brownish yellow or dun.","Particularly of color: dull, uninteresting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"},{"title":"Drab (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Drab is a dull, light-brown color. It originally took its name from a fabric of the same color made of undyed, homespun wool. The word was first used in English in 1686. It probably originated from the Old French word drap, which meant cloth. In 1897 the Sears catalog listed household paint colors including drab, light drab, Quaker drab, and olive drab."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Beige_wool_texture.jpg/330px-Beige_wool_texture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped